# Veripsa release gate (auto-discovered). One gate per file -> two PRs adding gates add two
# FILES, never a shared line -> no false merge conflict on registration. register_gate is
# defined in run_gates.sh. Format: register_gate <test> <marker> <name> <ok_blurb> <desc> [tail]
# NOTE: NO backticks and NO dollar-sign in the desc/blurb text below (shell-eval fragility -- see CLAUDE.md).
register_gate "tests/test_policy_change_refresh.py" "POLICY-CHANGE REFRESH GATE: PASS" "policy-change refresh (G4)" "policy-change refresh (G4): a committed policy write enqueues a content-free refresh row for that tenant IN THE SAME TXN as the policy commit; a background drainer re-derives ONLY that tenant's open in-flight PRs under the new policy, OUTSIDE any outbox transaction (idempotent re-post, skips merged/closed), and is generation-fenced against an uninstalled/revoked install" "policy-change refresh (G4): proves enqueue coalescing (rapid writes collapse to one pending row, epoch climbs), ROLLBACK-safety (a rolled-back policy write leaves NO outbox row -- negative control), FORCE-RLS tenant isolation of the outbox (another tenant's pin sees zero of an account's rows -- negative control), claim/finish CAS on the epoch, fail then bounded give-up, the generation/uninstall fence (revoked install never drained), the owner-account no-op, and at the drainer layer that ONLY the writing tenant's repos are refreshed (a bystander tenant with open PRs but no policy change is untouched -- negative control), that no GitHub call happens while an outbox transaction is open (seam), and that a dead install is skipped" 24
